#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:14
msgid ""
"Checks that this computer looks for updates, installs them, and gets them "
"from the right place."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:16
msgid ""
"Updates checks how updates reach this computer: how often it looks for them, "
"whether it installs them by itself, whether security updates are waiting, "
"where security updates come from, and whether installed software is left "
"without any source of updates.\n"
"\n"
"It reads how the computer is set up, not what an update program shows, so it "
"says the same whichever program you use for updates.\n"
"\n"
"The full report, and Home at Thorough, also check the package files: every "
"program installed from a package comes with a checksum for each of its "
"files, and every file is compared with it, so a changed or missing file "
"shows up, whoever changed it. Your own settings in /etc are not counted. "
"This reads tens of thousands of files, can take several minutes, and needs "
"the administrator password. A clean result means no changes were found, not "
"that the computer is proven clean: the checksums are not signed once "
"installed.\n"
"\n"
"Updates changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:31
msgid ""
"Most attacks use problems that already have a fix. A computer that does not "
"install its updates keeps those problems open, often for weeks, and security "
"updates matter most."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:35
msgid ""
"The report is grouped by what can go wrong: looking for updates, installing "
"them, where security updates come from, software no source keeps up to date, "
"package systems that are not checked, and, in the full report, package files "
"that were changed. Each problem is marked with a warning and leads on to "
"what to do about it."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:48
msgid "Check how updates reach this computer"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:58
msgid "Checking the package files needs the administrator password."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/plugin.c:59
msgid ""
"Checking how updates reach this computer… The package files can take a few "
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/private-files/plugin.c:14
msgid ""
"Searches your whole home folder for keys, passwords and other secrets that "
"others could read."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/private-files/plugin.c:16
msgid ""
"Private Files looks for secrets in your home folder, and in other folders "
"you add: private keys, password databases and stored logins, wherever they "
"are, for example a key copied to the desktop. For each one it looks at who "
"besides you can read it, taking every folder on the way into account. A "
"secret only you can read is normal, such as your SSH keys; one others can "
"read is a warning.\n"
"\n"
"It reads only the start of small files to recognise them, never shows their "
"content, and keeps nothing: the list lives on screen only. It needs no "
"password. It changes nothing unless you ask it to fix a file, and then only "
"takes others' access away."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/private-files/plugin.c:26
msgid ""
"A key or password file others can read can be copied without you noticing, "
"and gives access to what it protects: servers you log in to, your accounts, "
"your passwords. Old copies count too: a key from a machine you no longer use "
"may still open a server today."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/private-files/plugin.c:30
msgid ""
"Folders to Search: your home folder is always searched. Add folders "
"elsewhere on this computer or on a network, such as a disk with old backups; "
"the file manager's places outside your home folder are listed too, and each "
"can be removed from the list. Everything under each folder is searched, "
"within its own disk.\n"
"\n"
"Read Files Up To: files up to this size have their start read, to recognise "
"a key in a file of any name. Larger files are recognised by name only. "
"Smaller is faster on large disks; even the smallest holds every real key "
"file.\n"
"\n"
"Search Caches Too: caches are left out unless this is on. Programs rebuild "
"them and they seldom hold secrets, but they can take long on large disks."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/private-files/plugin.c:42
msgid ""
"The report lists the secrets found: private keys, password databases and "
"stored logins, grouped by who besides you can read them. Each one others can "
"read is marked with a warning and leads on to a fix that makes it readable "
"by you only. Those only you can read are listed so you know where they are.\n"
"\n"
"The notes at the end say which folders were searched, where the search "
"stopped before the end, and what it left out."
msgstr ""

